# Avere Navbar — Original Design (baseline)

When the user asks to restore “မူရင်း design” / original navbar, use this baseline — **not** the full-bleed dark sliding-pill header.

## Visual shell (keep these)

- `sticky top-0`, `rounded-2xl`, `backdrop-blur-xl`
- Light/dark glass: `bg-white/60` → scrolled `bg-white/90`, dark `bg-slate-900/70` → `bg-slate-900/90`
- Border: `border-white/30 dark:border-slate-700/50`
- Padding: unscrolled `py-5` / scrolled `py-3`, horizontal `px-7 lg:px-10`
- Soft shadow; slight scale shrink on scroll (`~0.985`) is OK

## Brand accent (signature)

- Top gradient bar on the nav card:
  - `absolute top-0 left-0 w-[88%] h-2`
  - `bg-gradient-to-r from-[#1e293b] via-[#475569] to-[#86adb4]`
  - `rounded-t-2xl`, animate `scaleX` from 0 → 1 on mount
- Soft inner wash: `bg-gradient-to-b from-white/40 … dark:from-slate-800/30`

## Layout

- Logo left (`/myphoto2.jpg`, rounded-xl, shrinks slightly when scrolled)
- Desktop links right: Home, Solutions & Services (dropdown), Product (wide dropdown), News & Events (dropdown), About us, Contact us, then auth
- Same i18n keys / AuthContext / publiccategory Product dropdown behavior
- Mobile: Menu/X + expandable accordion panel (same structure as before)

## Allowed enhancements (on top of baseline)

- Underline hover/active on links
- Dropdown `AnimatePresence` fade/stagger
- Link entrance stagger
- Chevron rotate on open
- Do **not** replace with full-width opaque dark bar + sliding pill unless user explicitly asks for “another / modern” design again

## Do not

- Change menu routes or remove Settings / Login / Register / user menu
- Drop light-mode glass support (original supports light + dark)
